// Proofs for the identities identities.hana states, in the strategy
// language of docs/proving.md. An identity with no entry here is proved by
// `diagram` alone — this file holds exactly the claims that need direction.

// The right-hand side is written as the call it is, and the engine is not
// allowed to spend a sentence's definition on its own: say so.
proof identities::testing_a_test_by_name = inline diagram;

// The arm recomputes the very test its branch decided. The driver
// identifies the two computations — `view-value`, then `dedup` — and the
// case split on the one wire that remains decides both readings at once:
// η, spent deliberately, where no rewrite window could.
proof identities::specializing_a_tested_value = both(decide) cases(equal) diagram;

// The two unpackings of a coercion. Both grow the graph — they say a
// coercion as the program it is — so no list drives them and the proof
// names the one it wants. What follows is the ordinary decision procedure:
// once the branch is there, the branch layer takes it from both sides.
proof identities::as_bool_is_the_branch_it_makes = lhs(fire(as-bool-branch)) diagram;
proof identities::as_int_is_a_guarded_identity = lhs(fire(coercion-guard)) diagram;
proof identities::as_tuple_is_a_guarded_identity = lhs(fire(coercion-guard)) diagram;

// The commuting conversion, spent where a proof asks for it. The row grows
// the graph — it duplicates the region the branch grows over — so no list
// drives it and the proof names it; once the branch has moved past the
// `negate`, the two sides are the one diagram.
proof identities::what_follows_a_branch_runs_inside_it =
    lhs(fire(select-hoist)) diagram;
